# tests/bench/lsan.supp -- LeakSanitizer suppressions for `make asan`.
#
# zg_argv_vec: generated C mallocs one row per argv entry at startup and
# never frees them (src/gen/gen_c/gen_c_main.zen:156). That is DELIBERATE -- the
# rows live exactly as long as the process and the OS reclaims them -- so
# the leak is suppressed here, by name, rather than "fixed" in codegen.
#
# The SECOND deliberate startup block (the root arena state, top frame in
# generated main) is NOT in this file on purpose: LSan matches any frame,
# every allocation sits under main, and naming main here would silence every
# real leak. tests/bench/asan.sh allowlists it by top frame instead.
leak:zg_argv_vec
